Deleting Branches in Local as well as remote (if required):
===========================================================
Delete Local branch you don't want:
git branch -D <feature_branch/sub_branch>                      [Ex: feature/dummy-testmodule]

Delete remote branches you don’t want:
git push origin --delete <feature_branch/sub_branch>           [Ex: feature/dummy-testmodule]


Renaming the Branch:
===========================================================
[Make sure you are in main branch]

Rename the branch locally:  git branch -m <Old_Branch_Name> <New_Branch_Name>
                       EX:  git branch -m feature/playwrite-python  feature/test-frameworks

Delete the old branch from the remote:  git push origin --delete <Old_Branch_Name>
                                   Ex:  git push origin --delete feature/playwrite-python

Push the renamed branch to remote and set upstream: git push -u origin <New_Branch_Name>
                                                EX: git push -u origin feature/test-frameworks